.It Dv DQ_REASON_NAMEMAX
.Va ds_namemax
is 0.
.It Dv DQ_REASON_MODE
bits outside
.Dv S_IFMT
and the permission bits.
.It Dv DQ_REASON_TYPE
the
.Dv S_IFMT
bits are not the kind's
.Pq Dv S_IFREG .
.It Dv DQ_REASON_SETID
.Dv S_ISUID
or
.Dv S_ISGID
is set.
.It Dv DQ_REASON_BLKSIZE
.Va di_blksize
below the page size.
.It Dv DQ_REASON_SIZE
.Va di_size
above
.Dv OFF_MAX .
.It Dv DQ_REASON_TIME
a
.Va tv_nsec
outside 0..999999999.
.It Dv DQ_REASON_PATHCONF
.Va dp_valid
names a slot beyond
.Dv DQ_PC_NCOUNT .
.It Dv DQ_REASON_POLICY , DQ_REASON_RIGHTS
see
.Sx Policy .
.It Dv DQ_REASON_FLAGS
.Va dm_flags
holds a bit other than
.Dv DQ_MINT_F_WRITE ,
or
.Dv DQ_MINT_F_WRITE
with a policy whose
.Va dp_write
is not
.Dv DQ_EVENT .
.El
.Ss Policy
A
.Vt struct dq_policy
accompanies each object.
Stage 1b accepts
.Va dp_cache
.Dv DQ_CACHE_NONE
.Po
.Xr read 2
always posts; pages exist only while mapped or wired; the only switch for
whether
.Xr fstat 2
posts is
.Dv DQ_EVENTS_GETATTR
.Pc ,
.Dv DQ_CACHE_ATTR
or
.Dv DQ_CACHE_DATA
.Pq read 2 served from cached pages, see Sx Pages ;
.Va dp_write
.Dv DQ_DENY
or
.Dv DQ_EVENT ;
.Va dp_ioctl
.Dv DQ_DENY
or
.Dv DQ_EVENT ;
.Va dp_mmap_shared_write
.Dv DQ_DENY ,
or
.Dv DQ_ALLOW
with
.Va dp_write
.Dv DQ_EVENT ;
.Va dp_exec
.Dv DQ_DENY ;
.Va dp_lock
.Dv DQ_EVENT ;
.Va dp_deadline_ms
at least
.Dv DQ_DEADLINE_DEFAULT ;
.Va dp_events
a subset of
.Dv DQ_EVENTS_GETATTR | DQ_EVENTS_CLOSE ;
.Va dp_pad0
zero.
Anything else is
.Er EINVAL
with
.Dv DQ_REASON_POLICY .
.Va dp_rights_version
must be the
.Dv CAP_RIGHTS_VERSION
the controller built
.Va dp_rights
with, and the rights must be valid, or the reason is
.Dv DQ_REASON_RIGHTS .
The minted descriptor carries exactly
.Va dp_rights ;
a controller presenting a file as
.Xr open 2
would should pass
.Dv CAP_ALL_RIGHTS .
.Dv DQ_IOC_SETPOLICY
may later change
.Va dp_cache ,
.Va dp_ioctl ,
.Va dp_deadline_ms
and
.Va dp_events
only; the other fields and the rights must equal the minted values
.Po
.Va dp_write
fixed the descriptor's access mode
.Pc .
.Pp
The access mode of the minted descriptor is fixed at the mint, as
.Xr open 2
fixes it: it is
.Dv FREAD
unless
.Va dm_flags
holds
.Dv DQ_MINT_F_WRITE ,
which installs it
.Dv FREAD | FWRITE
and needs
.Va dp_write
.Dv DQ_EVENT .
A policy of
.Dv DQ_EVENT
without the flag serves writes through no descriptor yet, but its
descriptors post
.Dv DQ_OP_FSYNC .
.Ss Ioctls
All on the queue descriptor, group
.Ql j :
.Bl -tag -width "DQ_IOC_SET_QUEUE_DEPTH" -offset indent
.It Dv DQ_IOC_MINT Vt "struct dq_mint_args"
Mint an object of
.Va dm_kind
presenting
.Va dm_ident
under
.Va dm_policy ;
returns
.Va dm_object
and the descriptor
.Va dm_fd ,
or
.Er EINVAL
with the reason stored through
.Va dm_reasonp
when that pointer is not
.Dv NULL
(a failing ioctl copies its argument back to nobody; on success
.Dv DQ_REASON_NONE
is stored).
.Er ENOSPC
when the queue holds
.Va kern.dq.max_objects
objects,
.Er ENXIO
when it is closing.
.It Dv DQ_IOC_MINT_OBSERVER Vt "struct dq_observer_args"
Mint an observer descriptor, see
.Sx Observers .
.Er EINVAL
for a wrong version, an unknown flag or nonzero padding.
.It Dv DQ_IOC_REPLY Vt "struct dq_reply"
Answer an event; see
.Sx Events and replies .
.It Dv DQ_IOC_REVOKE Vt "struct dq_object_args"
Revoke an object: every pending and in-flight event fails with
.Er EIO ,
.Dv NOTE_REVOKE
fires on its
.Dv EVFILT_VNODE
